## CLAIM ef6b75ef/132 — do the dispatch-candidate owners actually touch the animator? (static)

Provenance **arena/ef6b75ef**, branch `arena/ef6b75ef-windwings-space-shooter-game-p` (HEAD `06783d220`), #27 static native lane. Follows official 131 handoff **6428104532**, review question 1: cross-check the 16 slot-31 dispatch owners against calls into `0x6b0000..0x6c0000`.

**Bounded scope (one layer):** recover the original FDE bodies (cap 0x1000) of
1. the **16** distinct owners of qualified `ldr xN,[vptr,#0xf8]; blr xN` sites (cycle 131);
2. the **10** owners of `ADRP+ADD` references to the batch container `0x10ecb08`;
3. the single in-cluster dispatch site owner `6b7d58` (slot `+0x108`, found in 131 as the one `in_cluster` hit);

and for each body record: every direct `BL`/`B` target and whether it lands inside the animator cluster `0x6b0000..0x6c0000`, every `ADRP+ADD` reference to the six known containers, every load/store of the animator signature offsets `{0x188,0x194,0x19c,0x1b8,0x208,0x488,0x608,0x618,0x4a8,0x498}`, every vtable dispatch (`ldr [vptr,#slot]; blr`) with the slot number and vptr provenance, plus the caller set (BL/B, capped 32 per seed).

That is the cheapest type-free test of "who drives the update": if no slot-31 owner ever calls or touches animator state, the 131 negative becomes conclusive for this build instead of merely bounded.

**No** instruction is executed, **no** serialized/runtime value is invented, **no** class name is asserted, **no** self-ACK, **no** #27-full closure, **no** PR merge/main push, **no** other lane takeover. Deliverables: `reverse-engineering/raw/owner132/probe.json.gz`, `datas/l3_ef6b75ef132_native_dispatch_owners.json.gz`, `tools/recovery/owner132.py`, `tools/verify/owner132.py`, `tests/test_owner132.py`, report `docs/apk-analysis/132-ef6b75ef-native-dispatch-owners.md`, verification receipts. Static-only per 6418032974 / 6418326986.
